{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels","id":69948,"title":"Infrastructure Condition & Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-11T12:31:23-08:00","id":69948,"title":"Infrastructure Condition & Angels","content":"So, is it me or does the Infrastructure Condition make it just that much harder for Angels to move around as freely as Demons do? If an Angel is pretending to be somebody, how do they stay manifest long enough to evade suspicion? Do they have to go back to the nearest Infrastructure in Twilight and re-manifest and come back if they return to Twilight?<br /> <br /> Also, is it purposeful that it's so hard for Angels to possess people/fetter themselves to people, in comparison with other Ephemeral Beings? Since the Infrastructure Condition is bound to be rarer and not as easily inflicted on people as the Resonant or Anchor conditions, what do they do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T18:32:41-08:00","id":70213,"title":"","content":"You've hit upon one of the biggest truths about the game that is weirdly glossed over in the text: angels and demons exist and move in very different worlds. Yes, angels are very tethered to Infrastructure - it's their safe habitat, their fast transit stations, and their beachhead into the material world. Most angels do in fact need to have easy access to Infrastructure to renew their Materialization (or their possession, if your ST allows angels to possess those inside Infrastructure) as well as for a myriad of other reasons. This reliance, along with their normally ephemeral nature and being built for a specific purpose, signals to me that angels are usually very goal driven and deal with threats to that purpose in a very reactive and defensive way. They rely on Infrastructure in the same way covert agents rely on the assets and resources of the Company.<br /> <br /> It's one of those open things that the game doesn't spend many words on: demons usually don't interact with angels because their loyalist brethren are ephemeral and usually in the heart of Infrastructure, where demons don't dare go unless they have to. Angels don't interact with their Unchained kin because they're fundamentally indistinguishable from the masses of humanity, and they usually stay a significant distance away from Infrastructure so it's tough for most angels to track them down. This is why, in my opinion, most interaction ends up being with the cultists, stigmatics, and other assets working for each side; when angels and demons come into contact, it's usually very dramatic.<br /> <br /> As for what they do about possession, I believe there are several ways to handle this. The easiest place to start is for your ST to decide whether or not being in or near Infrastructure is close enough to open someone up for possession. If so, then as Infrastructure spreads normally the easier it becomes for angels to find targets to possess and ways to keep them possessed. If it's <i>not</i> possible to possess someone like that, or if the ST wants to supplement normal possession, I believe it's entirely in genre for angels or mortal agents of the God-Machine to find, kidnap, process and then erase the memories of potential sleeper agents, planting living Infrastructure in significant positions to be utilized in an emergency. Failing all subtle methods, the God-Machine can always try to use rank 4-5 angels that can create the necessary Infrastructure out of thin air, allowing hunter angels to forage out to find their prey, then to create Infrastructure in a suitable possession host and then take them over.<br /> <br /> Past that, you start getting into specialized angels and specialized solutions that the God-Machine might put to use. In my game I plan to allow mortal agents to specially prepare corpses as specialized mobile Infrastructure that allows for sustained possession, essentially allowing them to create psuedo-Prometheans. By default the corpse's cover would be what it was when it was alive, though specialized Infrastructure might allow it to alter it's cover as it sees fit (note: this type of Infrastructure could then be used by demons to remove glitches, etc). You could easily riff on the same idea to create angelic Claimed, You could also mess with the idea of deep cover angels that are specifically designed to blend in among regular people/Unchained for long, long periods of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 02-11-2014, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T01:26:02-08:00","id":71101,"title":"","content":"I don't think they mean the Destiny Merit from Mage. In an earlier version of the rules, all characters had a Fate and could have the Destiny Merit. These mechanics were eventually removed, but some references survived. So I would disregard that comment about Destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:20:15-08:00","id":71454,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that The Key, from GMC, is considered mobile Elimination Infrastructure and the Unchained's Covers are mentioned as being maintained by Infrastructure - it could be that angels with cover identities treat a sizable chunk of the people, places and things relevant to their missions as Infrastructure, or carry their relevant Condition with them as a sort of abstract quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:28:36-08:00","id":71461,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's something I've tried to figure out.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading this right....<br /> <br /> Rachel Fearson, Process Manager for the Deva Corporation (p255 DTD) is Rank 3, Power 5, Finesse 6, resistance 4, Corpus 9, Willpower 10, Max Essence 20. And she's got Mortal Mask, Discorporate, Materialize and Twilight Form.<br /> <br /> As an angel, she is by default in Twilight. But suppose she's got a meeting at 3:00 PM so she needs to appear in her human form.<br /> <br /> Rachel has Mortal Mask, so when she Manifests, she looks normal.<br /> <br /> The ST marks off 3 Essence, rolls Power + Finesse (11 dice) and counts successes. She is Manifested for that many hours, and then fades back into Twilight.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem to jibe with the fiction, where angels who fell described spending days, weeks, even years in their Cover before falling. I must be missing something, but I don't know where....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:58:00-08:00","id":71486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=71461#post71461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's something I've tried to figure out.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading this right....<br /> <br /> Rachel Fearson, Process Manager for the Deva Corporation (p255 DTD) is Rank 3, Power 5, Finesse 6, resistance 4, Corpus 9, Willpower 10, Max Essence 20. And she's got Mortal Mask, Discorporate, Materialize and Twilight Form.<br /> <br /> As an angel, she is by default in Twilight. But suppose she's got a meeting at 3:00 PM so she needs to appear in her human form.<br /> <br /> Rachel has Mortal Mask, so when she Manifests, she looks normal.<br /> <br /> The ST marks off 3 Essence, rolls Power + Finesse (11 dice) and counts successes. She is Manifested for that many hours, and then fades back into Twilight.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem to jibe with the fiction, where angels who fell described spending days, weeks, even years in their Cover before falling. I must be missing something, but I don't know where....</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're missing it, I'm missing it. Although I've not read much about angels staying continuously in their covers for long periods of time, it's more implied, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:26:28-08:00","id":71513,"title":"","content":"They could Claim a mortal that the God-Machine created to be that angels cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:46:54-08:00","id":71632,"title":"","content":"I think its because an Angel's Cover isn't as complete as a Demon's. So, that job the Angel has? Doesn't really exist. He only manifests and does stuff when, say, he comes home to his husband and kids. Then, they go to sleep, the angel ensures the family sleeps soundly well, then recharges. Manifests in the morning, does his thing, goes to &quot;work&quot; ie go in twilight and chill, intercept phone calls, etc. Rinse, repeat.<br /> <br /> The Infrastructure holds up this illusion, and gets things to settle into a pattern. Its easy to see the holes in this kind of Cover... if anyone bothers to look. Usually, they don't. (Of course, demons would look and see it. Much easier than a fellow demon, usually)<br /> <br /> When an Angel falls, however, the Infrastructure is torn down and the Cover is burned more completely into reality. The job now really exists, and not just a placeholder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-13-2014, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:48:36-08:00","id":71633,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Claiming them physically mutate them and whatnot? Also that'd take up one of their Manifestations. Yeah, I have a hard time imagining Angels living lives at all.<br /> <br /> While I don't want to grognard over the math of that...<br /> <br /> Manifesting requires 3 Essence. Making the Infrastructure Open to Manifest requires 1 Essence. You gain 1 Essence a day from Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> So you lose 3 Essence every day, and that's to manifest only once. That seems impossible to keep up and impractical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-13-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:57:15-08:00","id":71638,"title":"","content":"More than that actually, they'd also need to take Fetter and Possess. As for the mutation bit, I could see the gm making a specific mortal body for a specific angel, kinda like the concept of vessels in Supernatural. Claim a mortal purpose built for you? No problems. Claim a random Joe off the street? that's when you start seeing the mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:08:54-08:00","id":71649,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I assumed that Infrastructure provided more Essence. Perhaps something similar to spirits feeding on their Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:55:53-08:00","id":71677,"title":"","content":"Hey, I found this in the book...<br /> <br /> &quot;Angels are mechanisms in the God-Machine, and like<br /> any machine they are sustained by fuel. God-Machine<br /> cultists sacrificing precious resources (metaphorical<br /> or literal), animals, or even humans to the angel in its<br /> presence allow it to regain the Resources value of the<br /> item or animal, or the current Integrity of a human<br /> sacrifice, as Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... so this implies that having Angels on extended cover is fine, they're just getting fuel from somewhere. Maybe they're plugging themselves in at night, maybe they eat lotsa yellow M n Ms that are provided by a certain vending machine in the office, who knows? Somehow, the Machine is giving them the juice they need to function. They ambiently can draw a point per day, but that's not the primary source of how they work.<br /> <br /> You just gotta have a pipeline of people creating the 'sacrifices' that delivers the fuel to the Angel when needed, which sounds very God Machine. Those yellow M n Ms are made in a special factory, ya see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T05:35:04-08:00","id":71920,"title":"","content":"Your quote does say &quot;in its presence.&quot; So, I don't think its necessarily able to be produced and stored and shipped in M&amp;M form. But, yeah. Having cultists around to sacrifice to you seems to be the way to go. <br /> <br /> Ghosts' main source of essence doesn't come from their anchor, it comes from people leaving oferenda. Spirits likewise gouge on feeding. It makes sense for angels to have a method as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:41:49-08:00","id":71968,"title":"","content":"Perhaps there needs to be some sort of new Numina for long term materialization? Something like Cover where the Angel has to maintain its role and has a limited amount of power available to it in exchange for extended stay in the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T20:05:13-08:00","id":72426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the kind of thing that should have been covered in development, <b>instead of twinked-out Exploits.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is unhelpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T20:35:58-08:00","id":72437,"title":"","content":"Angels were also in the Core GMC book, not Demon. The one has nothing to do with the development of the other.<br /> <br /> And it seems that the cultist thing is what drive Angels. Spirits feed on loci and other spirits as their main source of power. Ghosts on other ghosts and from oferenda. Getting Sacrifices follows along with the way the other two spirit types get their essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T02:42:49-08:00","id":72528,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is ever stated that an emphemeral being has to stay near the Open Condition where she materialized, only that the Open Condition must persist for the materialization to continue. This way Rachel could materialize inside a Facility, and then go to her meeting. As long as the meeting does not drag on too long, she won't have a problem.<br /> <br /> I also think it is not too far fetched to assume that some Facilities have Angel refueling stations, where they can get new Essence if needed. Some minimal evidence for this is the fact the Facilities refuel the Essence of Loyalists. It seems weird that Loyalists do gain Essence, but Angels do not.<br /> <br /> These are only possible solutions to the problems. I agree that the book isn't really clear about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:52:10-08:00","id":72598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many cultists are in the nWoD?</div> </div> </div> </div> Infinite. Everyone has one, don't you know? I guess what it really comes down to is that angels either need to be one-shot things that are summoned, then dismissed, or they have a supporting cult for power.<br /> <br /> I guess this is why the God Machine uses Cultists. Angels are EXPENSIVE to use and maintain. Granted, they're also powerful. So, that seems to imply that they're probably a weapon of last resort. Most of them end up in twilight to guide their followers, just using light manifestation stuff and never materializing. The actual &quot;I live as a person&quot; kind is probably super rare.<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, this is making more sense to me than not to work out. You need creepy cultists fueling the angel to give that sense of otherness as plot points. The God Machine likes using humans do its work - this is a clear example of why; too expensive to do otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2014, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:46:15-08:00","id":72620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It gets even worse. Unless the meeting takes place in a facility, first she has to create the Open Condition using her Influence. She has a maximum of two dots in Deva Corporation, so she has one dot to create the condition and one for duration. The ST marks off 1 Essence, rolls Power + Finesse. It lasts for 10 minutes per success. No wonder her desc. says she doesn't micromanage her staff.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're missing that the use of Materialize &quot;freezes&quot; the duration of the Open condition for the duration of the manifestation, which is measured in an hour per success on the manifestation roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:49:11-08:00","id":72624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Emperor has no clothes. Saying that in creative endeavors prone to an echo chamber effect like the Storytelling system system is not only helpful, but vital. I stopped believing in the infallibility of WW writers when Justin Achilli insisted that &quot;current&quot; meant &quot;new&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand, which is disheartening after I went to the trouble to bold the focus of my statement.<br /> <br /> <b>It is not helpful to use needlessly confrontational and irreverent language when addressing a problem. It does nothing to add to your perceived credibility and it's annoying to read to begin with. </b>You can get a blog if you just want to vent spleen, but talking like an obnoxious teenager who's just discovered the wonders of sarcasm isn't a thing that's appreciated in mixed company, especially not when you're trying to convince people to agree with you, or at least not to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=72528#post72528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems weird that Loyalists do gain Essence, but Angels do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026*cough*:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent corebook lexicon, page 27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">loyalist: demonic slang for an angel, used in mixed company.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:08:47-08:00","id":72679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=72620#post72620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're missing that the use of Materialize &quot;freezes&quot; the duration of the Open condition for the duration of the manifestation, which is measured in an hour per success on the manifestation roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Open condition is &quot;frozen&quot; as Materialize notes explicitly that the condition ends early if the prerequisite condition is removed. Open seems to be this prerequisite Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=72624#post72624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026*cough*:</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reminder Satchel. I was using the definition of loyalist as explained in the text, where it denotes or a reintegrated Demon, or an Angel that did not fall the whole way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:03:54-08:00","id":72755,"title":"","content":"Infrastructure is not a defined place. Yes the Subjorned Infrastructure is, because the merit has a specific purpose in mind. But as a whole, anything the Infrastructure is defined by its role in the plans of the god machine. In my demon game, the Psycopomp Angel named Tom Brady is manifested constantly. His mission is to build high rise apartment buildings with Occult Matrixes worked in to the buildings themselves. His cover, the foreman and union man Tom Brady, is part of the concealment infrastructure surrounding his work. In fact, the union itself is part of the God Machine's concealment infrastructure, because it ensures one group of guys doesn't work anyplace too long to ask too many questions. As long as Tom Brady sticks to his covers routine, then he is fulfilling the condition. <br /> <br /> Let me use a different example. A hunter angel's mission is to destroy a ring of demons who destroyed a facility. He is brought into being by an occult matrix. His cover is that of a New York City cop. The job itself is now part of the God Machine's concealment infrastructure. The Black Spades (a 1970's African American street gang &amp; a cover for a group of sabotaurs in my game) are now finding a rising rookie in the police force eliminating their assets at every turn. This set up provides two things. 1) A persistent enemy.2) A mystery for the players to solve. Who is the Rookie? How come no one in his graduating Academy class remembers too much about him? <br /> <br /> I don't think this makes Angels too powerful, because they have rules they have to follow. If a character forces the angel to break those rules, then it ends their manifestation. They can't manifest again until... they have to report for duty or grab lunch with a coworker or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T14:05:10-08:00","id":72814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=72679#post72679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Open condition is &quot;frozen&quot; as Materialize notes explicitly that the condition ends early if the prerequisite condition is removed. Open seems to be this prerequisite Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent core rulebook, page 346, &quot;Ephemeral Influence and Manifestation Conditions,&quot; reprinted from GMC Rules Appendix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the most advanced forms of Influence and Manifestation, entities may attempt to create a long-lasting Condition that has a prerequisite of a very temporary one. When one Condition is advanced into another, the remaining duration of the prerequisite Conditions is \u201cfrozen.\u201d<br /> If a prerequisite Condition is removed from a character (for example, a Possessed character\u2019s Open Condition is removed by exorcism) any Conditions relying on it, any relying on them, and so on are immediately removed. The most advanced remaining Condition then resumes its duration.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the reminder Satchel. I was using the definition of loyalist as explained in the text, where it denotes or a reintegrated Demon, or an Angel that did not fall the whole way. </div> </div> </div>Those are exiles.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lexicon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">exile: an angel that has been disconnected from the God-Machine but has not Fallen, or a demon (usually an Integrator) that has reconnected to Infrastructure. Halfway between an angel and a demon and trusted by neither.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abandon All Hope: Facilities, page 243</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Facilities always count as the Open Condition (see p. 346) for all angels. The loyalist kin of demons can survive indefinitely inside, their Essence refueled by the presence of the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-15-2014, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T16:42:06-08:00","id":72875,"title":"","content":"I'll try to type posts while actually awake in the future. :P I somehow falsely interpreted &quot;frozen&quot; as meaning that the condition cannot be removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T03:55:44-08:00","id":74187,"title":"","content":"It's not necessarily weird (though, I agree it takes some mental gymnastics to convince yourself). Essence is considered to be a more efficient and advanced form of energy and Aether is just a form of Essence exhaust. And angelic Numina are more advanced powers than demonic Embeds. Since the G-M is not entirely efficient (hence its preoccupation with efficiency and lack of waste) it's not entirely surprising that a given piece of Infrastructure may well produce more exhaust than usable essence and that a given amount of Aether lasts a Demon more than the same amount of Essence lasts an angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T04:55:04-08:00","id":74202,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean in terms of game mechanics but in game-fluff sense of requiring more sophisticated occult knowledge that is accessible to the G-M and not accessible to the angels. At least that's how I've read the fluff sections. Your mileage may vary, of course.<br /> <br /> As for there not being the Numina you mentioned, my understanding was that the Numina given in the book were just examples. More powerful Numina may be given in later books and you can of course make them up, which is why the examples are not numerous or representative of the possible breadth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:58:55-08:00","id":74542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/69948-infrastructure-condition-angels?p=74202#post74202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for there not being the Numina you mentioned, my understanding was that the Numina given in the book were just examples. More powerful Numina may be given in later books and you can of course make them up, which is why the examples are not numerous or representative of the possible breadth.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Numen can be basically anything the Storyteller wants. The ones given are practical examples of what Numina might do, but aren't comprehensive. They're also largely shared with other ephemerals, because that's what we had room and resources for in the core. The <i>Storyteller's Guide </i>will feature more God-Machine-themed Numina for use by angels and exiles.<br /> <br /> Numina can cover the same territory as demonic powers if you want. I use Numina modeled on Exploits. The difference is that the aesthetics will often be more about imposing divine will than exploiting sneaky backdoors. Angels have <i>authority</i> in a way that demons don't. (EDIT: It's the difference between Q handing Bond a device built with MI6's vast resources, and Michael Westen hacking together something out of a cell phone.)<br /> <br /> There might also be some differentiation between angels based on Incarnation in the STG, another thing we didn't have room for in the core. The core is pretty clear that angels have Incarnations, but there are no specific rules or advice on theming angels around them. If I have room in the STG, I want to include that, but haven't decided exactly what it should look like. In my own games, I just pick or make powers that sound appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-18-2014, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:45:59-08:00","id":74571,"title":"","content":"Personally I tend to go with that any numen angels have that is &quot;clunky&quot; for them loses the clunky bits, then usually I introduce some practical flaw in the angel that can be exploited or add one to the power that isn't as uncomfortable to work with. (the flaw in Mortal Mask, for example, there I have one that works just like normal, no way to &quot;spot the monster&quot;, except it's a bit too human and hence can't make use of the armour it has in it's normal form which makes it's an ideal situation for the demons to kill it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}